Ticket #4471 was merged as one known issue and queued as one fix. The reports in it are not one cause.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

`parser` is the shared date parser. It reads every date month first. A day-first tenant's dates come out flipped: the month and the day trade places.

`hint` is the booking-v3 form. The hint under the field says `MM/DD/YYYY`, so people type the month first. The form then reads that text the tenant's way, day first. Same symptom, different bug. The table marks it as not this ticket: it has no ticket of its own.

A parser fix does not correct the hint. A hint fix does not correct the parser.

<Callout kind="warn">
Five reports were read as a one-day move. They stay in the count of the cause they were filed under. The note under the table is that reading.
</Callout>

